To fully replace LEAF’s native header/menu/footer in Template Editor, make main.tpl and main_iframe.tpl minimal wrappers that:

include your universal header script (/launchpad/files/leaf_header.js)
keep LEAF-required content containers (#content / #bodyarea)
remove/omit native header/menu includes
optionally leave menu.tpl unused (or reduce it to empty/minimal)
Recommended implementation pattern
1) Put your files in a stable shared location
You already did this:

/launchpad/files/leaf_header.js
/launchpad/files/leaf_header.css (self-loaded by JS)
Good—single source of truth.

2) Replace main.tpl shell
In main.tpl, remove legacy header/nav rendering and include only:

<script src="/launchpad/files/leaf_header.js"></script> (ideally near </head> or before </body>)
LEAF content region expected by app pages (important: keep id contracts your JS extractor uses)
Your JS currently extracts in this priority:

[data-lp-content]
#content
#bodyarea
<main>
So keep #content and/or #bodyarea in template output for compatibility.

3) Replace main_iframe.tpl similarly
Use the same lightweight shell + script include for iframe-based views, unless you intentionally want the iframe template to be headerless.

Given your router/modal behavior, keeping consistent structure across both templates prevents edge-case regressions.

4) menu.tpl options
Since your header renders nav itself, you have 2 safe choices:

Best: stop including menu.tpl from main.tpl/main_iframe.tpl.
Fallback: keep include but make menu.tpl empty/minimal no-op.
Do not keep legacy menu HTML active, or you’ll get double-nav and conflicting behavior.

5) Keep LEAF-required internals intact
Even with a full visual replacement, don’t remove template placeholders that server-side pages depend on (title vars, content injection vars, scripts/styles hooks, etc.).
Your header hides #header/#footer already, but for a complete replacement you should remove their rendering from tpl, not just hide with CSS.

Practical “minimal shell” shape (conceptual)
Use this structure in both template files:

Head:
existing LEAF-required meta/title/css/js hooks
your one line:
<script src="/launchpad/files/leaf_header.js"></script>
Body:
keep skip/content landmarks expected by LEAF pages
keep #content and/or #bodyarea wrapper where LEAF injects page body
no legacy top nav/header/footer markup
Important gotchas (for LEAF specifically)
Don’t delete required Smarty vars/placeholders
Strip chrome markup, not framework placeholders.

Launchpad detection
Your JS enables router only on lp_home/#lpSwapHost. Ensure launchpad template/page still renders the marker you rely on.

Cross-app routes (iframe: true)
These are correct in your config. Don’t force those into fetch/splice.

menu.tpl references in old pages
Some old templates may include menu.tpl directly. Grep for includes and neutralize those paths too.

Cache/static asset invalidation
After replacing templates, clear LEAF/template cache and hard refresh browsers; otherwise you’ll think tpl edits “didn’t take.”

Rollout strategy (safest)
Clone current main.tpl, main_iframe.tpl, menu.tpl backups.
Apply replacement in lower env.
Validate:
standard report pages
launchpad hash routes
iframe routes (CoP, Ideas, Help Library, Privacy)
modals, skip link, keyboard nav, breadcrumb behavior
Promote to prod with rollback-ready backups.
